  "result": "Excellent! All 133 tests pass (including the 17 new payment tests). Here's what I've implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Created `src/payments.js`** with:\n- `recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })` \u2014 Records a payment on an issued or partially_paid invoice. Updates the invoice status to 'paid' when fully covered, or 'partially_paid' otherwise.\n- `balanceDue(invoice)` \u2014 Calculates the total amount still owed (invoice total minus all payments).\n\n**Added error codes to `src/errors.js`:**\n- `NOT_ISSUED` \u2014 Can only record payments on invoices with status 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n- `OVERPAYMENT` \u2014 Payment exceeds what's owed\n\n**Validation:**\n- Amount must be a positive integer (cents)\n- Payment cannot exceed the balance due\n- Creates the `payments` array if it doesn't exist\n\n**Created `test/payments.test.js`** with 17 tests covering:\n- Payment recording on issued and partially_paid invoices\n- Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n- Error cases (NOT_ISSUED, AMOUNT_INVALID, OVERPAYMENT)\n- Balance calculations with multiple payments\n- Edge cases (missing payments array, fully paid invoices)",
